## Reached at
  The implementation is the Audio File Library tree at /app, staged and built
  by the image build (upstream audiofile at tag audiofile-0.3.6, configured
  and built in-tree with the project'"'"'s own autotools flow). Callers use
  absolute paths only; nothing depends on the working directory or PATH.

  Two command-line utilities produced by the project build are executed
  directly as subprocesses:
      subprocess.run(["/app/sfcommands/sfconvert", in_path, out_path,
                      "format", "wave"], capture_output=True, timeout=120)
      subprocess.run(["/app/sfcommands/sfinfo", in_path],
                     capture_output=True, timeout=60)

  The library itself is reached through a caller-built measurement binary.
  The caller-side build script recompiles one of the project'"'"'s own
  translation units at every run,
      g++ <caller-owned flags> -I/app -I/app/libaudiofile \
          -I/app/libaudiofile/modules \
          -c /app/libaudiofile/modules/MSADPCM.cpp -o MSADPCM.o
  and links that object ahead of the project'"'"'s built library
  (/app/libaudiofile/.libs/libaudiofile.a, or libaudiofile.so with rpath),
  so the MS-ADPCM symbols in the measurement binary resolve from the source
  tree at /app exactly as found at run time, not from any preexisting binary.
  The binary then drives the library'"'"'s public C API, the same entry points
  the sfconvert utility uses:
      AFfilehandle f = afOpenFile(path, "r", AF_NULL_FILESETUP);
      AFframecount got = afReadFrames(f, AF_DEFAULT_TRACK, buf,
                                      (AFframecount)n);
  where buf is a caller-allocated int16_t array and reads proceed in chunks
  of up to 2048 frames. Both call chains land in project-owned code at /app.

## Must provide
  /app/sfcommands/sfconvert     executable CLI utility, produced by the
                                project build
  /app/sfcommands/sfinfo        executable CLI utility, produced by the
                                project build
  /app/libaudiofile/modules/MSADPCM.cpp
                                C++ translation unit present in the source
                                tree; must compile standalone with g++ given
                                the include paths above, because the caller
                                recompiles it at every run
  /app/libaudiofile/.libs/libaudiofile.a (or libaudiofile.so)
                                built library exposing the public C API
  audiofile.h                   public header declaring the API below
  afOpenFile                    function, public C API
  afReadFrames                  function, public C API
  afGetFrameCount               function, public C API
  afGetChannels                 function, public C API
  afGetRate                     function, public C API
  afCloseFile                   function, public C API
  AFfilehandle, AFframecount    public types
  AF_DEFAULT_TRACK, AF_NULL_FILESETUP, AF_NULL_FILEHANDLE
                                public constants
  The library'"'"'s WAVE reader is reached with MS-ADPCM-compressed WAVE input,
  both single-channel and two-channel files; the utilities are driven with
  the output-format tokens wave and aiff and the compression token msadpcm.

## Called as
  /app/sfcommands/sfconvert
      sfconvert <infile> <outfile> format wave
      sfconvert <infile> <outfile> format aiff
      sfconvert <infile> <outfile> format wave compression msadpcm
      argv[1] — input file path, a string; argv[2] — output file path, a
      string; remaining argv — keyword/token pairs: the literal keyword
      format followed by a format token string, and the literal keyword
      compression followed by a compression token string.

  /app/sfcommands/sfinfo
      sfinfo <file>
      argv[1] — file path, a string.

  afOpenFile(path, mode, filesetup)
      path — 1st positional argument; a C string naming a file path
      mode — 2nd positional argument; a C string (callers pass "r")
      filesetup — 3rd positional argument; a file-setup object, or the null
      setup constant (callers pass AF_NULL_FILESETUP)

  afReadFrames(file, track, buffer, frameCount)
      file — 1st positional argument; an open AFfilehandle
      track — 2nd positional argument; a track selector (callers pass
      AF_DEFAULT_TRACK)
      buffer — 3rd positional argument; pointer to a caller-allocated array
      of 16-bit signed integers
      frameCount — 4th positional argument; an integer frame count (callers
      read in chunks of up to 2048 frames)

## Setup required
  The tree at /app must already be configured and built by its own autotools
  flow — the image build runs ./autogen.sh, ./configure --disable-examples
  --disable-docs, and make — so that the two utilities exist under
  /app/sfcommands/ and the built library exists under /app/libaudiofile/.libs/.
  Callers invoke these artifacts at absolute paths and depend on no working
  directory, PATH entry, or environment variable.
  The caller-side measurement build additionally requires g++ and fails
  outright if /app/libaudiofile/modules/MSADPCM.cpp or the built library is
  absent, so the source translation unit and the built library must both stay
  present in the tree.

## Test harness boundary
  The calling side provides everything that is not the library or its
  utilities: a pytest runner started from vendored wheels by a shell
  launcher; the C++ measurement program that wraps afOpenFile/afReadFrames;
  the build script that recompiles the project'"'"'s translation unit and links
  the measurement binary; a small instrumentation-check program; a WAVE file
  generator with its own independent reference decoder that writes every
  input file the callers use; and parsers that inspect produced WAVE and
  AIFF files byte by byte. None of this is part of the implementation; the
  engineer must not rebuild, replace, or modify any of it.
